Z||000000||William||12-31-2000||10:53 AM||||My new Black / Tan interior project is proceeding nicely. Just be picked up a mint dash that will get coated with black SEM on the next warm day. The dash has the nicer map pocket, but it is gray. I'm gonna drop the pocket in a bucket of black dye to color the cloth part of the pocket. As I here that some plastics will accept the dye if the water is hot and some vineger is added, I'm hoping the the vinyl cup part will take the dye?(It's already charcoal in color.) I don't think the SEM paint would look good on the pocket and I hope that I can just dye it. My other choices are to paint one of those glove boxes black or see if Mr Mike will contruct a black pocket using leather. AS this is a nice pocket, I would rather use it if I can just color it black. Thoughts?||||reg||1
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||12-31-2000||11:15 AM||||  William, I recolored my whole interiort rim with SEM Color Coat system, including the dash and dash pocket. It turned out great. The SEM Color Coat system is designed specificaly for that kind of material, I wouldn't use it on carpeted pieces though. I think that by dropping the whole thing in water you might distort or warp the underlayment, which I believe is cardboard. I sent one to Mr.Mike and he is going to look into covering it in matching leather to match my seats and door panels. It shouldn't be any harder for him than the door pockets. Just my "OPINION" I would try the SEM first and see how you like it. Later I will replace mine with Mr.Mikes leather.<P>  Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 12-31-2000).]||||reg||12
